[juj]: I do recall that coming up in the past. https://linux.die.net/man/3/usleep mentions that

```
4.3BSD, POSIX.1-2001. POSIX.1-2001 declares this function obsolete;
use nanosleep(2) instead. POSIX.1-2008 removes the specification of usleep().
```

Nanosleep should exist in Emscripten. We could consider emulating `usleep`, though quickest is probably to convert to `nanosleep`.

