[kripken]: Ok, code looks good, let's just figure out the test issue. How did you add it that it didn't work?

It might make sense to add it alongside the other `test_embind_*` tests in `tests/test_core.py` - looks like we don't have an embind test with memory growth there yet (otherwise we could just add to it).

---

[beakbeak]: I was able to fix my original attempt at adding a test, which runs as part of `other.test_embind`. I was using an existing function called `force_memory_growth()`, which only gets compiled with `-O2` and becomes a no-op. I modified the function to use `_malloc()` and `_free()` instead of `new` and `delete[]` so that the allocation doesn't get optimized out.

